; Quests: what a quest IS. Where the party has got to is SAVE state
; (WorldState::quests), never here — a catalog describes the world, and a
; catalog that also remembered your progress could not be shared between saves.
;
; Fields:
;   display   the quest's name.
;   stages    ORDERED stage ids, earliest first. A quest ABSENT from the save
;             has not started, which is why there is no "not started" stage to
;             author and forget.
;   text_<stage>   one line describing that stage. Read by whatever asks what
;             a quest wants next; there is no journal screen yet.
;
; Content reaches a quest through an ITEM (items.cat `quest = <id>:<stage>`),
; which is the hook the design actually asked for: "you might find a quest item
; in a dungeon. This will update some quest flags for the overall world."

[sunken_relic]
display = The Sunken Relic
stages = heard found
text_heard = A carved token names a relic somewhere below the crypt.
text_found = The relic is in your hands.
